{"id": "rl-001", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "The mid-term will be held in class on October 17th; that is also in your syllabus.", "events": [{"date": "2007-10-17", "kind": "test"}], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "plain, real", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-002", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "The mid-term is on October 17th, which is a Wednesday, in class.", "events": [{"date": "2007-10-17", "kind": "test"}], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "weekday confirms the date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-003", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "All right, the problem sets: there will be roughly ten problem sets and I'll talk about them more later. The first one will go out on Monday but it will be due ten days later.", "events": [{"date": "2007-09-20", "kind": "assignment"}], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "Monday + ten days later", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-004", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "Roughly speaking they'll be every week.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "recurring, no event", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-005", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "Please don't anybody tell me late - any time after today you didn't know when the mid-term was.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "midterm + today, but nothing to calendar", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-006", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "Five things you learnt today, hand in your numbers and the legal forms and I'll see you on Monday.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "hand-in is immediate; Monday is just goodbye", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-007", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "There is a Midterm and there is a Final.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "no dates", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-008", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "The Final will not be held in the exam period, because I like to take long vacations. It will be held the last day of class.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "no date known for the last day of class", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-009", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "Prior to the exams I will post previous exams online, so you have a feeling for how these exams work and so on.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "no event", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-010", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "There is a book review, a short book review, to be written towards near the end of the class. I'll give details about that later on in the semester.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "vague, no date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-011", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "And I'll start with the topic that we'll be covering next week on Monday - the brain.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "lecture topic, not a deadline", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-012", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "And I'll introduce the teaching fellows sometime next week.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "vague", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-013", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "Let's see, there's already a problem set posted on the Classes server. And it is due next Friday, a week from Friday.", "events": [{"date": "2011-09-09", "kind": "assignment"}], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "next Friday restated as a week from Friday", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-014", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "Today's lecture includes an examination of Hurricane Irene that hit Connecticut a few days ago on August 28.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "'examination' is not an exam; past date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-015", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "And last year, our final exam was on the first day of exam period.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "last year, past", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-016", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "And now we're on the last day of exam period, December 17. You have to be here on--I forget what day of the week that is.", "events": [{"date": "2011-12-17", "kind": "test"}], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "this year's final: Dec 17", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-017", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "But I will tell you that the labs are on Monday and Tuesday afternoon.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "recurring labs", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-018", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "So we'll be doing those lab sign ups next week when you have a better idea of what your schedule is like.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "class-run activity, vague", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-019", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "Now the labs aren't going to start actually until week three.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "no calendar date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-020", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "These are dates along, August twenty-third, twenty-fourth, twenty-fifth, twenty-sixth, so on.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "hurricane data dates, no event", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-021", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "That was taken twelve hours later, 00Z on the twenty-eighth and 00Z on the twenty-ninth.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "satellite image times, past", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-022", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "Now - but today is January 15th, it is Martin Luther King's birthday.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "today, nothing to calendar", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-023", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "Okay, we'll have more on Thursday.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "next lecture, recurring", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-024", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "I will put it up, this afternoon we'll get it up on the Web, through the Registrar's site or however.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "teacher-side, today", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-025", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "This was of course August 1963.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "historical month-year", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-026", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "I know it fits - 10:30 on Tuesday, Thursday - a hundred other reasons - you want a lecture course.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "class meeting times", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-027", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "In one year, the year I have statistics for, 1999, there are 174 acid attacks in Bangladesh.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "bare year and a count", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-028", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "Then about six million years ago another group came off and they evolved into humans.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "deep time", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-029", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "As I mentioned, the females come into estrus only about once every six years after their last young was born.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "every six years is not a date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-030", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "We will continue on Thursday and I'll set up sections in between, and any questions?", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "next lecture", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-031", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "In 1665, 93% of the people that died in that year died of infectious diseases.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "historical year and percentage", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-032", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "We're going to spend quite of bit of time talking about it during the third week of the course.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "course week, not a calendar date", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-033", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "There are no lab reports that are due.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "negated", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-034", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "It's a fully implantable artificial heart, and it was introduced about seven or eight years ago now.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "years ago", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-035", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "I'll see you on Thursday hopefully.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "goodbye", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-036", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "Game Theory is a method of studying strategic situations.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "game theory"}], "actions": [], "note": "plain spoken definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-037", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "This kind of game is called a \"coordination problem\" and we'll revisit it later on in the semester.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "named but not explained", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-038", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "The main textbook is this one, Dutta's book Strategy and Games.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "is-statement, not a definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-039", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-09-05", "text": "One thing I can guarantee from past experience in this class, is that the median grade will be a B+.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "grading talk", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/economics/econ-159/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-040", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "A knot is a nautical mile per hour.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "knot"}], "actions": [], "note": "crisp real definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-041", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "And GOES stands for Geostationary Environmental Satellite.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "GOES"}], "actions": [], "note": "acronym expansion", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-042", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "A Gedanken experiment is a thought experiment, comes from the German word for thought.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "Gedanken experiment"}], "actions": [], "note": "", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-043", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "Climate is defined usually as kind of average weather.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "climate"}], "actions": [], "note": "hedged definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-044", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "We call it nowcasting. It's like forecasting except it's forecasting for just the next few minutes.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "nowcasting"}], "actions": [], "note": "term then meaning in the next sentence", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-045", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2011-08-31", "text": "I'm Professor Ron Smith from the Department of Geology and Geophysics.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "introduction, not a definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/geology-and-geophysics/gg-140/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-046", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "Cotard's syndrome is you believe that you're dead; you are persuaded that you're dead.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "Cotard's syndrome"}], "actions": [], "note": "spoken, unusual grammar", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-047", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2007-01-17", "text": "This is a brain.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "deictic, not a definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/psychology/psyc-110/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-048", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "This is what we call a sexual dimorphism that males and females are taking different evolutionary routes.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "sexual dimorphism"}], "actions": [], "note": "we call + run-on explanation", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-049", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "There's something called sperm competition where she may want to have a whole variety of different sperms.", "events": [], "definitions": [{"term": "sperm competition"}], "actions": [], "note": "something called X where Y", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-050", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2009-01-12", "text": "There's a whole group of beetles called dung beetles.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "named group, not a definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/molecular-cellular-and-developmental-biology/mcdb-150/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-051", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "Scientists observe and try to describe and engineers try to design.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "contrast, not a term definition", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-052", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "This is a picture of London Bridge, it's an interesting bridge which is important in the history of London.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "aside", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-053", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-15", "text": "Books are precious things.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "opinion", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/history/hist-119/lecture-1"}
{"id": "rl-054", "lang": "en", "locale": "en-US", "ref": "2008-01-14", "text": "That study is Systems Physiology and that's an important subdivision of Biomedical Engineering.", "events": [], "definitions": [], "actions": [], "note": "named but not explained", "src": "oyc.yale.edu/biomedical-engineering/beng-100/lecture-1"}
